Makruk piece artwork attribution
=================================

This directory holds two sets of CC BY-SA 4.0 Makruk piece SVGs from two
different artists. OpenMakruk currently ships the Fulmene set
(`makruk/`); the Yevrowl silhouettes are kept around as a minimalist
fallback / reference set.


Active set: public/pieces/makruk/
---------------------------------

  white_king.svg, black_king.svg
  white_queen.svg, black_queen.svg     (Makruk Met = queen role slot)
  white_bishop.svg, black_bishop.svg   (Makruk Khon = bishop role slot)
  white_knight.svg, black_knight.svg   (Makruk Ma)
  white_rook.svg, black_rook.svg       (Makruk Ruea)
  white_pawn.svg, black_pawn.svg       (Makruk Bia)

Source:   Fulmene / makruk-pieces-image
          https://github.com/Fulmene/makruk-pieces-image
Author:   Fulmene
License:  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
          (CC BY-SA 4.0)
          https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

These are turned-wood-style Makruk pieces drawn in Inkscape with linear
gradients for highlight/shadow — the "3D" look that resembles physical
Makruk sets. Files were renamed to match chessground's piece role
slots (king/queen/bishop/knight/rook/pawn × white/black). Contents are
unmodified except for the rename.

The originals (with Fulmene's filenames khun_w.svg, met_w.svg, etc.)
plus a copy of their LICENSE file live in public/pieces/fulmene/.


